# Justified exceptions for scripts/verify-doc-links.sh.
# Format: <substring>  # <reason>
# Every non-comment line MUST carry a `# reason`, or the gate exits 2.
# Do not add an entry to silence a real broken link - fix the link.

references/api-endpoints-auth.md      # illustrative example in create-skill/references/token-efficiency-criteria.md, not a file in this repo
references/api-endpoints-payments.md  # illustrative example in create-skill/references/token-efficiency-criteria.md, not a file in this repo
references/api-endpoints-users.md     # illustrative example in create-skill/references/token-efficiency-criteria.md, not a file in this repo
references/api-patterns.md            # illustrative example in create-skill/references/writing-effective-instructions.md, not a file in this repo
references/ffmpeg-encoding.md         # illustrative example in create-skill/SKILL.md showing a hypothetical skill layout

docs/playbooks/git.md  # deliberately deprojected (docs-architecture R13); this repo correctly has no such file, but docs/workflow-harness/migration.md must name the exact path so consumers upgrading past the deprojection can delete their stale copy. Permanent, not a deferral.

CLAUDE.md  # global path `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` cited by setup/README.md and skills/rules prose; not a repo file

docs/research/cli-config-patterns.md  # illustrative example in librarian/references/examples.md showing where a cited research report is saved, not a file in this repo
docs/plans/active/cli-orkit.md        # illustrative example in create-cli/references/examples.md showing where a CLI spec plan is saved, not a file in this repo

